  "description": "GUHRAE crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C64 H129 Cr3 Dy3 N3 O27. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Cr1 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Cr2 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Cr3 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.323-4.014 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.25-113.62°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C64H129Cr3Dy3N3O27. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 3 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
